<title>ITALY: Genoa sets city water/gas utility float range.</title>
<headline>Genoa sets city water/gas utility float range.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Genoa said it has fixed a price range of 1,150 and 1,300 lire per share for the flotation of its AMGA SpA water and gas utility.</p>
<p>The public sale offer relates to a maximum 159.7 million shares, equal to 49 percent of the utility owned by the city.</p>
<p>Merchant bank Mediobanca is the global coordinator for the utility's privatisation and stock exchange listing by end-1996 and Banque Paribas is financial adviser.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
</text>
